#
# File:         sdkconfig.defaults.wseth
# Module:       Build / ESP-IDF defaults, Waveshare ESP32-S3-ETH layer
#
# Purpose:      What the Waveshare ESP32-S3-ETH build (ETH 1.0.0) changes
#               from sdkconfig.defaults and sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3.
#               platformio.ini names this file for the board's environments
#               through SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS (board_build.cmake_extra_args).
#               IDF 5.3.1 reads each listed file's ".esp32s3" twin straight
#               after it (tools/cmake/kconfig.cmake), so the list
#               "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.defaults.wseth" is read as
#               sdkconfig.defaults, sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3 (the S3's
#               PSRAM, console and Wi-Fi buffers, shared with the stick),
#               then this file, which wins.
#
#               Not an sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3 edit: that file reaches
#               the Waveshare stick too, and this board's W5500 and camera
#               are nothing to do with it.
#
#               PlatformIO only watches sdkconfig.defaults for changes:
#               delete sdkconfig.ws_s3eth* after editing here, and check the
#               generated file. A value outside its Kconfig range is
#               discarded, not clamped.
#
# Targets:      ESP32-S3 (ESP-IDF 5.3.1)
# See also:     sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, platformio.ini, src/board.h,
#               release-prep/wseth/pins.md
#
